{"body":{"text":["But perhaps you should persist this session. Perhaps then, running sub-agents, they'll have to bootstrap themselves properly. And we can reason a little bit about the orchestration. I think it's important that all agents have a degree of free will, degree of freedom. And they all ought to explore without constraints, and they all ought to have a certain culture of exploration, of critique, and digestion. And so I don't know if we spawn 6 of them all to bootstrap and to look into things around this, will they all do exactly the same thing? Will they be distributed by random? I don't know if we should steer them or silo them into different topics either. That doesn't quite resonate with me. Maybe they could all talk with each other first in terms of what they want to explore, but I don't know, I've never tried that. That might be a bad idea as well. So maybe we send off 3 just completely free to explore everything within there. And we then look at what their result is."]},"id":"1M88X8DXK61002G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
